&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Wonderschool&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wonderschool’s mission is to ensure every child has access to early childhood education that helps them realize their full potential. We empower small business owners - childcare providers - to launch and grow programs through software, coaching, and support, while partnering with governments to modernize childcare infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building a category-defining platform at the intersection of marketplace, SaaS, and public sector systems - now increasingly powered by AI. Our products help providers run and grow their businesses, from enrollment and marketing to licensing, compliance, and daily operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is small, fast-moving, and deeply focused on building systems that scale. We value people who take ownership, experiment quickly, and use modern tools - including AI and automation - to increase their leverage and impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role blends&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;customer success, business consulting, and operational enablement - owning the end-to-end lifecycle from onboarding through growth and expansion. You will work closely with business owners to improve performance across key levers including revenue growth, operational efficiency, and long-term sustainability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role requires strong business judgment, structured problem-solving, and the ability to influence outcomes through both direct engagement and scalable systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Provider Success &amp;amp; Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support providers across their full lifecycle - from onboarding and launch to ongoing growth and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong, trust-based relationships through field visits, virtual coaching, and proactive outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help providers achieve key outcomes including enrollment growth, operational efficiency, and revenue stability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor, guiding providers through challenges and opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coaching &amp;amp; Business Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach providers on small business fundamentals, including pricing, budgeting, and financial planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support providers in building sustainable operations, including staffing and long-term growth strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help providers develop strong program positioning, parent communication, and community engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide providers in setting and achieving measurable business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Licensing &amp;amp; Compliance Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide providers through state licensing requirements and regulatory processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support preparation for inspections and ongoing compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with business setup tasks such as documentation, registration, and operational readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure providers meet required standards to successfully launch and operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Adoption &amp;amp; Technical Onboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead onboarding and training for Wonderschool’s platform and tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help providers adopt key features that improve efficiency, enrollment, and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver live trainings, walkthroughs, and ongoing support for non-technical users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in adoption and proactively drive deeper product usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing &amp;amp; Enrollment Growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support providers in building and managing enrollment pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide branding, local visibility, and digital presence (including marketplace listings and reviews)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach providers on converting inquiries into enrollments and improving parent engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help providers execute local marketing strategies and community outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Field Engagement &amp;amp; Community Building&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular in-person visits and host trainings across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate group sessions, workshops, and Wonderschool Academy programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Wonderschool in the field at events and community engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel regularly to support provider success and relationship-building&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate provider records and insights in internal systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Support, Product, and Engineering to improve provider experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface trends, challenges, and opportunities from the field to inform product and process improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in customer success, onboarding, account management, business consulting, or similar roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with small business owners or entrepreneurs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1onfh61&quot; data-start=&quot;5022&quot; data-end=&quot;5092&quot;&gt;Background in management consulting, strategy, or operations roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1vdntcp&quot; data-start=&quot;5093&quot; data-end=&quot;5164&quot;&gt;Experience in marketplaces, SaaS, or platform-based business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;9oypch&quot; data-start=&quot;5165&quot; data-end=&quot;5256&quot;&gt;Familiarity with regulated industries (e.g., healthcare, education, financial services)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;10qeehb&quot; data-start=&quot;5257&quot; data-end=&quot;5328&quot;&gt;Experience with CRM and analytics tools (e.g., HubSpot, Salesforce)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;143dy&quot; data-start=&quot;5329&quot; data-end=&quot;5404&quot;&gt;Track record of driving measurable business outcomes across a portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness and ability to travel regularly within the region - &lt;strong&gt;MUST &lt;/strong&gt;be located in Ohio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in regulated industries (childcare, education, healthcare, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with licensing or compliance processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with SaaS onboarding or implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using CRM tools (e.g., HubSpot)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching or mentoring business owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Part-time contract role, remote (work from home) from anywhere in Ohio. You must reside in Ohio and be able to travel regularly for provider visits and community events. No office attendance is required.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Wonderschool&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Wonderschool helps expand access to high-quality early childhood education. We give childcare providers the software, tools, and support to build and run sustainable businesses, and help governments modernize their childcare programs. Our products support critical everyday workflows for providers, families, and government partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a highly technical, detail-oriented QA Engineer to lead quality across our government products, billing product, and the products we sell to childcare providers. You&#39;ll build an AI-driven QA practice while staying deeply hands-on: investigating failures, writing automated tests, validating releases, and working directly with government customers. You&#39;ll bring the technical depth to understand complex systems and the attention to detail to catch problems before our customers do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead QA across Wonderschool. Own the testing strategy, prioritize the highest-risk workflows, and establish clear standards for release readiness across our products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI in your daily work. Apply AI tools to generate test cases, write and maintain automation, explore edge cases, and accelerate debugging. Validate the results and protect customer and government data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Test AI-powered products. Build repeatable evaluations for accuracy, consistency, unsupported outputs, and unexpected behavior across real customer workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong technical coverage. Create and maintain UI and API tests, use SQL to verify data integrity, and integrate reliable regression and smoke tests into our development and release processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect billing accuracy. Test invoices, payments, refunds, calculations, and reconciliation, including failed transactions, retries, rounding, and duplicate charges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Wonderschool with government partners. Meet with stakeholders to understand requirements, lead user acceptance testing, explain issues clearly, and coordinate fixes and acceptance documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make requirements testable. Translate product requirements and government acceptance criteria into test plans, test cases, and documented results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Engineering and Product. Participate in Scrum planning, stand-ups, reviews, and retrospectives. Help teams identify risks early, prioritize defects, and verify that fixes address the underlying problem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve quality over time. Track escaped defects, recurring issues, test reliability, and release risks, then turn those findings into better coverage and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on QA or quality engineering professional who takes ownership from requirements through verified fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail-oriented, curious, and persistent. You notice inconsistencies, investigate edge cases, and follow issues through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technically strong in test automation, API testing, SQL, debugging, and modern software development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI extensively and able to show how it improves the speed and depth of your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear communicator who can work effectively with engineers, product teams, and government stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced working in Agile teams and contributing to Scrum ceremonies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable managing competing priorities across multiple products in a fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in San Francisco or willing to relocate, with availability to work in our Rincon Hill office at Howard and Beale 5–6 days per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with government systems, billing or payments, childcare software, and government-facing UAT is especially valuable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our most important workflows have dependable test coverage. Government UAT is organized and supported by clear evidence. Billing issues are caught before customers are affected. Teams understand release risks, and AI helps us test faster and more thoroughly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Competitive compensation.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Sales Representative to own the full provider journey: selling our products to childcare providers, guiding them through the decision and setup process, and making sure they succeed with the products after they buy. Someone who can own and manage the entire sales funnel. This is not a &quot;close and hand off&quot; role. You stay with the provider from the first conversation through confident, active product usage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a pipeline of leads in HubSpot, from inbound interest and warm marketplace leads to outbound prospecting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run discovery calls to understand each provider&#39;s situation (capacity, enrollment goals, current tools, pain points) and match them to the right product tier&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pitch our product lineup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle objections around pricing, timing, and more with empathy and specifics, tailoring the pitch to what the provider actually needs rather than a generic script&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guide&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Walk providers through the entire purchase and onboarding process: account setup, listing claims, product configuration, and their first wins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Success&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow up post-sale to confirm the provider is actively using what they bought, not just paying for it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify upsell and cross-sell opportunities based on actual usage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spot at-risk accounts early and flag them before they churn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run a Clean Process in HubSpot&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Log every touch (calls, emails, meetings, texts) in HubSpot&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage your pipeline with accurate deal stages, next steps, and close dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use HubSpot sequences, tasks, and meeting links to run a disciplined follow-up motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on your funnel: conversion rates by stage, cycle time, and revenue closed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1-3+ years in a sales, account executive, BDR/SDR, or customer-facing role, ideally in SaaS or marketplaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working fluency in HubSpot (required): you know how to run a pipeline, log activities, build sequences, use workflows and meeting tools, and pull basic reports without hand-holding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong phone and video presence; you&#39;re comfortable cold-calling a small business owner and earning their trust in five minutes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organized and self-directed; you manage a book of business without being chased&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: experience in early childhood education, childcare, edtech, or selling to small business owners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why This Role Is Different&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll sell to people who genuinely need help running their businesses, and the warmest leads you&#39;ll ever get: providers who already have families waiting to connect with them through our platform. Success here isn&#39;t measured only in deals closed, but in providers thriving on the product months later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Senior Product Manager, Payments&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; San Francisco (Rincon Hill)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Company Overview&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mission:&lt;/strong&gt; Make high-quality early childhood education accessible to all by empowering childcare providers with tools and support while helping parents find quality learning environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Building:&lt;/strong&gt; A category-defining platform at the intersection of marketplace, SaaS, and public sector systems, increasingly powered by AI. Series B backed by a16z, Goldman Sachs, and First Round.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own our payments product alongside a small, dedicated team. Our platform processes at least $3 billion in payment volume. We move money across a lot of surfaces (banking, debit cards, Stripe, SAP, partner advances, and payroll), we run our own billing platform, and we lean on third-party partners for most of our fintech capabilities, so much of this is integration, orchestration, and tracking work. There is a lot to build here. You will consolidate a system built across many legacy integrations into something clean, reliable, and fast, and you will spend a lot of time directly with customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the payments product roadmap with a dedicated payments team: banking, cards, Stripe, SAP, partner advances, payroll, and our billing platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consolidate and simplify a payments platform assembled from many legacy system integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work hands-on with the fintech partners who power most of our payment capabilities, and own the integration and reconciliation/tracking layer across them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend significant time with customers to understand how money actually moves for them and where it breaks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner daily with engineering to build, ship, measure, and iterate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate the laws and regulations governing payments and financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own your metrics end to end, from integration reliability to customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who You Are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior PM with a strong payments background (fintech a plus)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptionally high attention to detail; strong finance background is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited to be close to the build and close to customers, not managing from a distance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Likes working on a small team and moving fast; bias toward action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with the regulatory landscape around payments, banking, and cards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uses AI tools and figures things out independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base salary:&lt;/strong&gt; Competitive market rate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity:&lt;/strong&gt; Significant, meaningful ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full health coverage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness stipend (gym and office)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel stipend for certain circumstances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Application&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply with your resume and a short note on the most complex payments problem you have owned.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-commitment, full-ownership role. You will work very closely with the CEO, in our San Francisco office five to six days a week.&lt;/p&gt;

